===== RAMDISK boot =====
This is for booting OpenWrt without touching the flash chip memory ([[#serial]] cable and tftp server in your PC required):
  - build your own firmware, specifically select the RAMDISK option when configuring via ''make menuconfig''
  - set the **192.168.1.7** static IP on your computer, and connect the ethernet cable to the router
  - put the xxxxxx-wndr4300-initramfs-uImage.bin into the TFTP server at your computer
  - boot the router and break into the Uboot command line, via serial console
  - enter the following into Uboot command line: <code bash>tftpboot 82000000 xxxxxx-wndr4300-initramfs-uImage.bin
bootm </code> 
  - The system should boot!

